course: dictionary
lesson: 2863
title: Domestic: many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means. «The domestic silk moth cannot fly properly and no longer lives in the wild; it depends on people completely.» The clue is no longer lives in the wild, so domestic here means tame and kept by people.
explain: Domestic can also mean to do with the home or family, like domestic chores such as cooking and cleaning. It can also mean inside one country, like domestic flights that do not leave the country. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a home, an animal or a journey?
explain: Some words are used as jokes. «"Domestic engineer" is a joking name for a housewife, househusband or homemaker.» Engineers usually build machines or bridges, but here it means someone who runs the home. Read the words around it, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Domestic means to do with the home or family, such as domestic chores like cooking and cleaning.
fact: Domestic animals are tame and kept by people, such as cats, dogs and cows. They are not wild.
fact: Domestic flights stay inside one country. They are not foreign.
fact: The domestic silk moth cannot fly properly and depends on people completely. Its caterpillars, silkworms, eat almost nothing but fresh mulberry leaves.
fact: Domestic violence means harm inside a family. It is serious: if you ever see it or feel unsafe, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The domestic silk moth cannot fly properly and no longer lives in the wild.» What does domestic mean here? | Angry and wild | *Tame, kept by people | Foreign, from another country | Very large and fast
exercise: Which of these is a domestic chore? | Flying to Spain | Sailing across the sea | Watching a film in a cinema | *Hoovering the living room
exercise: Ravi flew from Leeds to London, staying inside Britain the whole way. What kind of flight was it? | Foreign | *Domestic | Wild | Ancient
test: The name «domestic engineer» is used as a joke. What does it mean? | A servant from long ago | Someone who fixes trains | A kind of storm | *A person who runs the home
test: What is domestic violence? | A wild animal that lives in the woods | A chore done at home | *Harm inside a family, which you should tell a trusted adult about | A quarrel between two countries
exam: Read: «Her domestic flights all stayed within one country.» What does domestic mean in this sentence? | To do with cooking and cleaning | Tame and kept by people | An old word for a servant | *Inside one country, not foreign
